  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday Night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1140 AM CDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nExcessive heat will be the biggest weather concern for this week \nthanks to the broad ridge of high pressure dominating much of the \neastern CONUS. The worst of the heat will be Tuesday and\nWednesday, but temperatures will remain well above-normal with \nrain & storm chances very low to near zero. Only isolated showers\nor a storm are currently forecast across the higher terrain of \nthe Plateau mid to late week and this is influenced by an upper-\nlevel low moving (west) off of the Atlantic toward the Southeast\nUS. We'll have to wait until Sunday/Monday to see an improvement \nin temperatures and to get more viable rain chances which would be\nin association with an upper-level trough (mercifully) moving in \nfrom the west",
